<article class="env-lemma" id="094V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/094V">Lemma <span data-tag="094V">37.64.7</span>.</a> Let $X \to Y \to Z$ be morphisms of schemes. Assume that $X \to Y$ is flat and surjective and that $X \to X \times _ Z X$ is flat. Then $Y \to Y \times _ Z Y$ is flat. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider the commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[r] \ar[d] &  X \times _ Z X \ar[d] \\  Y \ar[r] &  Y \times _ Z Y }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       The top horizontal arrow is flat and the vertical arrows are flat. Hence $X$ is flat over $Y \times _ Z Y$. By Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02JZ" data-tag="02JZ">29.26.13</a> we see that $Y$ is flat over $Y \times _ Z Y$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>